<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Regni</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Regnenses</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Regni or Regnenses were the people of the Roman civitas centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/noviomagus-reginorum">Noviomagus Reginorum</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichester">Chichester</a>, in what is now Sussex. The area formed part of the client kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togidubnus">Togidubnus</a> after the Roman conquest of 43. Their name may mean the people of the kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/regni.jpg" alt="Regni" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: myself · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Britain.south.peoples.Ptolemy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
